  "name": "Liaison Sub-Committee on National Policy Statements",
  "parent_committee_id": 103,
  "purpose": "<p>When a Government Department lays a National Policy Statement before the House, Standing Order No. 152H requires the National Policy Statements sub-Committee of the Liaison Committee to meet to decide to either refer the Statement to an existing Departmental Committee, or to establish a dedicated Committee to consider the policy statement. The sub-Committee’s decisions can be found in the <a href=\"https://committees.parliament.uk/committee/103/liaison-committee-commons/publications/6/formal-minutes/\">Liaison Committee’s Formal minutes</a>.</p>",
